Third-party material in this repository
=======================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code written for this project:
uc1810c.py, ucd.py, ucapp.py, the files in ui/, the packaging scripts, the
tests and the documentation.

Two directories contain material under other licences.


vendor/ - PyUSB
---------------

PyUSB is Copyright (c) 2010-2024 Wander Lairson Costa and contributors, and is
distributed under the BSD 3-Clause licence. It is vendored unchanged (minus
byte-code caches) so the application needs no pip install at runtime and is not
affected by PEP 668. See vendor/LICENSE for the full text.


kernel/ - Linux kernel sources
------------------------------

The files in kernel/ are snapshots of Linux kernel sources and remain
GPL-2.0-only:

  mixer_s1810c.c    sound/usb/mixer_s1810c.c    (Nick Kossifidis)
  mixer.c           sound/usb/mixer.c
  quirks.c          sound/usb/quirks.c
  quirks-table.h    sound/usb/quirks-table.h

They are included as reference material for people extending this project or
porting it to another model. Nothing in this repository compiles, links or
imports them: studio-1810c is a userspace program that reaches the interface
through libusb. Each file's own copyright header is authoritative.


Vendor software is not redistributed
------------------------------------

No PreSonus or Fender binary, installer, driver or firmware appears in this
repository. The protocol documented in PROTOCOL.md was recovered from a copy of
Universal Control that the author is licensed to run, and from USB traffic
observed on hardware the author owns.
